{{Term/Store|Ancient Gear|Ancient Gears|Series, BotW, AoC|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="Inventory">{{Cite|{{Big|Ancient Gear}}<br/>A gear used in ancient machinery. Despite being incredibly old, its build quality is leaps and bounds above anything built using current technology.|Inventory|BotW}}</ref><ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Ancient Gear}}<br/>A gear used in ancient machinery. Despite being incredibly old, its build quality is leaps and bounds above anything built using current technology.|Spoils|AoC}}</ref>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
In {{BotW}}, Ancient Gears can be obtained by defeating [[Guardian]]s or finding them in [[Treasure Chest]]s. They are also sold by the [[Slippery Falcon (Tarrey Town Branch)]] and the travelling [[Merchant]] [[Teli]], who can be found on the road northwest of [[Hateno Village]]. As is the case with all [[Ancient Material]]s, Ancient Gears were made by the ancient [[Sheikah]] and used in their machinery. In spite of their age, they are still more advanced than anything else that exists during {{BotW|-}}.<ref name="Inventory"/>

Ancient Gears can be given to the [[Ancient Oven]] at the [[Akkala Ancient Tech Lab]] to make various pieces of [[Ancient Soldier Gear]]. Since they count as [[Monster Part]]s, they can be combined with critters in a [[Cooking Pot]] to make [[Elixir]]s. They can also be exchanged at the [[Fang and Bone]] for [[Mon]] or used as an ingredient for [[Gray Dye]] at the [[Kochi Dye Shop]].

Ancient Gears are required to upgrade the following pieces of [[Armor]] at a [[Great Fairy Fountain]].

{{Material Armors|BotW|Ancient Gear}}

